Application design baseline

The selected direction is a Windows-first offline modular monolith in C# on .NET 10 LTS. .NET 10 is currently an active LTS release with support through November 14, 2028. The CLI baseline uses System.CommandLine, which supplies Windows/POSIX parsing, help, completion, response-file support, and independently testable parsing behavior.

The selected integrations are still provisional until their spikes pass:

upright.exe
├── CLI host and machine-output renderer
├── configuration and capability probe
├── scan planner
│   ├── deterministic discovery
│   ├── file identity and fingerprinting
│   ├── metadata extraction
│   ├── bounded thumbnail decode
│   ├── EXIF display transform
│   ├── four candidate rotations
│   ├── face/landmark inference
│   ├── feature extraction
│   ├── calibrated decision policy
│   └── immutable SQLite plan
├── apply executor
│   ├── stale-input revalidation
│   ├── JPEG DCT or raster transformation
│   ├── metadata normalization
│   ├── independent verification
│   └── commit, journal, recovery, and backup
├── review workflow
└── jobs, reports, diagnostics, and undo

Windows ML is the preferred inference-runtime candidate because it supports local ONNX execution on Windows and execution-provider management across CPU, GPU, and NPU hardware. A self-contained deployment is possible, but it adds roughly 41 MB of runtime components, which is why package size and provider behavior are explicit spike criteria rather than assumptions.

ExifTool is the leading metadata adapter candidate. Its -stay_open protocol allows a process to remain loaded and execute synchronized commands without paying process-startup cost for every image. It still must pass licensing, maker-note, XMP/IPTC, timestamp, malformed-file, and round-trip tests before it becomes a final production dependency.

libjpeg-turbo is the leading JPEG transform dependency. It provides coefficient-domain lossless transformation capabilities, including an in-memory transform path, but edge dimensions that do not align with JPEG MCU boundaries require an explicit product policy—refuse, trim, partially transform, or re-encode. The application will never silently choose one of those fidelity tradeoffs.

Critical design decisions already made
Orientation is not aspect ratio

The engine does not decide merely whether a picture “should be portrait or landscape.”

It computes:

stored pixel orientation
+ metadata display transform
+ inferred additional quarter-turn
= normalized upright display

That distinction is critical because EXIF Orientation includes mirrored states, and a portrait display may be stored in a landscape-shaped pixel matrix.

scan and apply are separate operations

scan is read-only. It creates a sealed plan containing:

source identity;
source fingerprint;
metadata evidence;
model and runtime versions;
orientation evidence;
selected action;
confidence;
reason codes;
output expectations.

apply consumes that plan. Before modifying or copying anything, it confirms that the input still matches its scanned identity. Changed files are rejected as stale rather than processed against old evidence.

Abstention is mandatory

The decision classes include:

KEEP
NORMALIZE_METADATA
ROTATE_90_CW
ROTATE_180
ROTATE_270_CW
REVIEW
UNSUPPORTED
ERROR

A low-confidence result becomes REVIEW. The system will optimize precision before coverage.

The proposed release targets are engineering gates, not current claims:

accepted selfie precision of at least 99.5%;
false rotation of accepted already-upright images no greater than 0.1%;
coverage increased only after the precision gate passes;
no source-loss cases in the fault-injection matrix.
Safe-copy is the default

The standard operation writes corrected files to a separate destination. It does not overwrite the collection.

In-place operation requires:

explicit destructive-mode acknowledgement;
source revalidation;
verified backup;
write-ahead journal entry;
same-volume staging;
transform and metadata write;
independent reopen and verification;
atomic replacement;
durable completion record;
recoverable undo information.
No silent JPEG damage

For JPEG files, the preferred operation is a lossless coefficient-domain quarter-turn.

Where losslessness is impossible because of edge dimensions or an unsupported transformation, the policy must explicitly choose among:

route to review;
refuse;
permit disclosed trimming;
permit disclosed re-encoding under an explicit option.

No fallback may silently crop or recompress the image.

Privacy is structural

The core workflow:

runs offline;
does not require an account;
does not transmit images;
performs face detection, not identity recognition;
does not produce identity embeddings;
does not enable telemetry by default;
redacts paths in support bundles unless explicitly included;
verifies model and native dependency digests.
